From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bpereira <bpereira@cloudflare.com>
Date: Wed, 12 Aug 2026 16:50:25 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Fix missed damage and stale caches under incremental layout

Each of these left a node with stale style, boxes or layout once box
construction became damage-gated.

remove_node marked the parent's ancestors dirty and stamped damage, but
never put a RestyleHint on the parent itself, unlike its sibling
remove_and_drop_node. The traversal therefore reached the parent's
subtree without anything asking for a recascade, so every selector that
reads the parent's child list kept stale style after a removeChild:
:empty, :nth-child and :has all reproduce.

This is the detach-without-drop path that a DOM's removeChild and
Element.remove use, so page JS hits it directly.

`YieldData::InlineBoxBreak` binds the float's id as `node_id`, shadowing
the container the whole function is laying out; so the cache bust meant
for the container landed on the float box. The container it was written
to protect kept cache-hitting, and its floats never re-registered into
the block formatting context: a float in a sibling container held the
band position the first float had before it grew.

The float's id is `float_id` now, which is what the shadowing cost us.

Retire the flag where the node's boxes are rebuilt rather than latching
it for the document's life. The inline pass is the wrong place to clear
it: `float:none` restructures the content into anonymous blocks and the
old container never runs an inline pass again, so it would bust its
cache forever. A float change is box-tree damage, so the re-collect that
handles it is exactly the point the registration stops being true.

Under incremental layout, stylo computes RestyleDamage::RELAYOUT for
style changes that affect layout but not box structure (min-height,
width, height). The damage gate in resolve_layout_children only
re-collects for CONSTRUCT_FC | CONSTRUCT_BOX, so RELAYOUT-only nodes
keep their old layout_children but should still have their layout
recomputed. Taffy's cache is keyed on available_space and parent_size,
not on style, so a style change without a cache clear returns stale
layout.

1. propagate_damage_flags now clears node.cache when the damage
   contains RELAYOUT, in addition to ONLY_RELAYOUT | CONSTRUCT_BOX.
   Stylo's damage levels are cumulative masks: REPAINT,
   REBUILD_STACKING_CONTEXT and RECALCULATE_OVERFLOW are all subsets of
   RELAYOUT, so the test is contains(), not intersects(). Otherwise a
   transform or opacity change cleared every ancestor's taffy cache, and
   each CSS animation tick re-ran grid track sizing up the tree.
2. Table roots cache a TableContext during box construction that
   includes table styles (min-height, border-spacing). Under incremental
   layout this context never updates for RELAYOUT-only changes, so force
   CONSTRUCT_BOX on table roots with RELAYOUT and build_table_context
   re-runs.

Fixes table-grid-item-dynamic-002 and related incremental layout
regressions where dynamic style changes on tables were ignored.

border-spacing, border-collapse, caption-side and empty-cells are
inherited, and an anonymous table wrapper only ever picks them up from
its parent via style_for_anonymous during box construction.

compute_layout_damage did not look at the InheritedTable struct, so a
change to any of them fell through to bare RELAYOUT. The parent never
re-collected, create_anonymous_table never re-ran, and the wrapper kept
the border-spacing it was created with.

Stylo itself declares all four servo_restyle_damage="rebuild_box"; this
just stops blitz's hand-rolled damage from dropping that on the floor.

Inserting a node under a parent that is not yet on a dirty path left the
traversal blind to the new child, so newly inserted nested shadow
content was never styled or collected. Mark the parent's descendants
dirty on insertion so the next layout pass reaches the new children.

invalidate_inline_contexts damages every inline root so its text
re-shapes, but for an anonymous root it damaged only the layout parent.
That works for wrapper blocks, because the parent's re-collect frees and
rebuilds them. A pseudo-element is anonymous too, but it lives in the
element's before/after slot and the re-collect reuses it. So a block
whose only text is its own ::before kept the glyphs it shaped before the
webfont arrived. desmos.com's icons (<i> blocks and flex items with
::before content) painted as tofu for the whole session.

Damage the anonymous root itself as well as its parent.

An atomic inline's vertical-align becomes its parley
InlineBox::vertical_align when the box is constructed, so a change to
baseline-shift or alignment-baseline has to reconstruct the box. Without
it a vertical-align change left the box at its old shift.

Co-authored-by: Rui Figueira <rfigueira@cloudflare.com>
---
 src/layout/damage.rs | 43 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++---
 src/layout/inline.rs | 10 ++++++----
 src/mutator.rs       | 12 ++++++++++++
 src/resolve.rs       |  5 +++++
 4 files changed, 63 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/layout/damage.rs b/src/layout/damage.rs
index 5d8373a..b3e7531 100644
--- a/src/layout/damage.rs
+++ b/src/layout/damage.rs
@@ -113,6 +113,18 @@ impl BaseDocument {
             damage.insert(RestyleDamage::RELAYOUT);
         }

+        // Table roots cache a TableContext during box construction
+        // that includes the table's style (min-height, border-spacing, etc.).
+        // Under incremental layout, RELAYOUT damage does not re-collect, so the
+        // TableContext stays stale and taffy reads old styles. Force box
+        // reconstruction for table roots whenever their layout styles change.
+        if damage.contains(RestyleDamage::RELAYOUT)
+            && !damage.contains(CONSTRUCT_BOX)
+            && self.nodes[node_id].flags.is_table_root()
+        {
+            damage.insert(CONSTRUCT_BOX);
+        }
+
         // Compute damage to propagate to parent
         let mut damage_for_parent = damage; // & RestyleDamage::RELAYOUT;

@@ -144,8 +156,15 @@ impl BaseDocument {

         // If the node or any of it's children have been mutated or their layout styles
         // have changed, then we should clear it's layout cache.
+        //
+        // Stylo's damage levels are cumulative masks (REPAINT is a subset of
+        // RELAYOUT), so only `contains` means relayout. `intersects` cleared
+        // every ancestor's cache for a transform or opacity change, and each
+        // CSS animation tick re-ran grid track sizing up the tree.
         let mut invalidate_anonymous_ancestors = false;
-        if damage.intersects(ONLY_RELAYOUT | CONSTRUCT_BOX) {
+        if damage.intersects(ONLY_RELAYOUT | CONSTRUCT_BOX)
+            || damage.contains(RestyleDamage::RELAYOUT)
+        {
             node.invalidate_layout_cache();
             invalidate_anonymous_ancestors = true;
             damage.remove(ONLY_RELAYOUT);
@@ -398,6 +417,11 @@ pub(crate) fn compute_layout_damage(old: &ComputedValues, new: &ComputedValues)
             || old_box.position != new_box.position
             || old_box.contain != new_box.contain
             || old.clone_visibility() != new.clone_visibility()
+            // An atomic inline's vertical-align becomes its parley
+            // InlineBox::vertical_align when the box is constructed, so a change
+            // has to reconstruct it or the box keeps its old shift.
+            || old.clone_baseline_shift() != new.clone_baseline_shift()
+            || old.clone_alignment_baseline() != new.clone_alignment_baseline()
         {
             return true;
         }
@@ -406,6 +430,15 @@ pub(crate) fn compute_layout_damage(old: &ComputedValues, new: &ComputedValues)
             return true;
         }

+        // border-spacing/-collapse/caption-side/empty-cells are inherited, and reach an
+        // anonymous table wrapper only via style_for_anonymous at box-construction time.
+
+        // Stylo declares them servo_restyle_damage="rebuild_box"; without a rebuild here the
+        // parent never re-collects, so the wrapper keeps the values it was created with.
+        if old.get_inherited_table() != new.get_inherited_table() {
+            return true;
+        }
+
         if new_box.display.outside() == DisplayOutside::Block
             && new_box.display.inside() == DisplayInside::Flow
         {
@@ -527,10 +560,14 @@ impl BaseDocument {
             };

             if element.inline_layout_data.is_some() {
+                // A pseudo-element is anonymous too, but its parent's
+                // re-collect reuses it instead of rebuilding it like a wrapper
+                // block, so it must carry the damage itself. Without this, a
+                // block whose only text is its own ::before kept the glyphs it
+                // shaped before the webfont arrived (for example an icon font).
+                node.insert_damage(ALL_DAMAGE);
                 if node.is_anonymous() {
                     anon_nodes.push(node.id);
-                } else {
-                    node.insert_damage(ALL_DAMAGE);
                 }
             } else if let Some(input) = element.text_input_data_mut() {
                 input.editor.set_scale(scale);
